<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Use This Age Calculator</h2>
    <p>Select your date of birth using the date picker. The calculator automatically updates to show your current age the moment you pick a date. By default it calculates your age as of today.</p>
    <p>If you want to know how old you will be on a future date, or how old someone was on a past date, fill in the second field labeled "Calculate Age On This Date." This is helpful for verifying eligibility deadlines, retirement dates, or checking someone's age at a historical event.</p>
    <p>All processing happens in your browser. No birthdate data is sent to any server.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>How Age Is Calculated</h2>
    <p>Age calculation sounds simple but has a few tricky edge cases. The basic approach is: take the target date, subtract the birth year to get full years, then check whether the birthday month and day have passed yet this year. If they have not, subtract one from the year count.</p>
    <p>Month calculation follows the same logic. After accounting for full years, count how many additional complete months have passed since the last birthday. Days are whatever remains after the full months are accounted for.</p>
    <p>Leap year birthdays add a special case. People born on February 29 officially turn a year older on March 1 in non-leap years. This calculator applies that convention consistently.</p>
</section>

<section class="examples">
    <h2>Age Calculation Examples</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Standard age lookup:</strong> Born on April 15, 1990. As of July 25, 2026, that person is 36 years, 3 months, and 10 days old. Total days lived: approximately 13,249.</li>
        <li><strong>Retirement eligibility:</strong> Born on September 3, 1962. Full retirement age of 67 falls on September 3, 2029. The next birthday countdown helps track when that milestone arrives.</li>
        <li><strong>Pediatric checkup age:</strong> A child born January 20, 2023 is exactly 18 months old on July 20, 2024, useful for scheduling well-child visits.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal drinking age check:</strong> Born March 1, 2004. The person turns 21 on March 1, 2025. Any date before that they are still under 21.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

