<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>How old am I if I was born in a specific year?</h3>
    <p>A quick estimate: subtract your birth year from the current year (2026). If your birthday has not yet passed this year, subtract one more. For example, someone born in 1995 who has not had their 2026 birthday yet is 30 years old. Enter your exact date in the calculator for the precise years, months, and days figure.</p>

    <h3>What if I was born on February 29?</h3>
    <p>February 29 birthdays occur once every four years. In non-leap years, this calculator treats March 1 as the official birthday for age purposes, which is the most widely accepted convention for legal and administrative use.</p>

    <h3>Can I calculate someone's age on a specific past or future date?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Use the second date field to enter any target date. The tool will calculate the exact age between the birth date and that specific point in time. This works for both past and future dates.</p>

    <h3>Is the total hours count accurate?</h3>
    <p>The hours figure is calculated from total days and does not account for the specific time of day you were born. If you were born at 11 PM and it is currently 8 AM, the hours count may be off by several hours. For most purposes this level of precision is more than enough.</p>
</section>

